problem_statement:
Variable scoping broken in templates with blocks and loops

#### Description

Template variable scoping is not working correctly when using scoped blocks within loops or when including templates that reference loop variables. Variables that should be accessible in certain scopes are not being found, causing templates to render incorrectly or raise undefined variable errors.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```python
from jinja2 import Environment, DictLoader

# Case 1: Scoped block with loop variables
env = Environment()
tmpl = env.from_string('''
{%- for i in ["foo", "bar"] -%}
{% block body scoped -%}
{{ loop.index }}) {{ i }}{% if loop.last %} last{% endif -%}
{%- endblock %}
{% endfor -%}
''')
print("Expected: 1) foo2) bar last")
print("Actual:", repr(tmpl.render()))

# Case 2: Include with loop variables  
env = Environment(loader=DictLoader({
    'inc': '{{ i }}', 
    'main': '{% for i in [1, 2, 3] %}{% include "inc" %}{% endfor %}'
}))
print("Expected: 123")
print("Actual:", repr(env.get_template('main').render()))

# Case 3: Context passing with scoped blocks
from jinja2 import pass_context

@pass_context
def test_func(ctx):
    return f'{ctx["i"]}'

env = Environment()
tmpl = env.from_string('''
{%- set i = 42 -%}
{% for idx in range(2) -%}
{{ test() }}
{%- set i = idx -%}
{% block body scoped %}
{{ test() }}
{% set i = 24 -%}
{{ test() }}
{% endblock -%}
{{ test() }}
{% endfor -%}
{{ test() }}
''')
tmpl.globals['test'] = test_func
print("Expected: 42024024142124142")
print("Actual:", repr(tmpl.render()))
```

The variable resolution seems to be returning empty results or incorrect variable mappings in scoped contexts.

